  "id": "wf4-verify-channel-changed-after-the-gate",
  "description": "If the Approval Gate resolved a different channel than the verified register row, the branch halts.",
  "why_it_exists": "On the real MAT-20260101-002 snapshot the Actions register held TWO generations of rows written 39 minutes apart, so six action_ids each resolved to two rows carrying different action_types, recipients and channels. Approval Gate re-queried by action_id and simply took the last match, meaning WF4 could draft, approve and send against a row nobody chose - for example sending a CONTACT_INSURER letter to a car park manager. The Integrity Guard refuses to choose between duplicate rows, and Verify Selected Row re-checks the chosen row immediately before any writer or Gmail node runs. Channel is the second field that decides where a message goes; an action the register marks MANUAL must not be emailed.",
